// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-056
// title: EtherNet/IP Gateway (Allen-Bradley / Rockwell PLCs)
// date: 2026-04-03
// status: accepted

#context
Allen-Bradley ControlLogix / CompactLogix PLCs use EtherNet/IP (CIP) on TCP 44818.
Tags are named strings (e.g. 'Temperature_1', 'Program:Main.Pressure').
node-ethernet-ip provides Controller.connect(host, slot) + readTag(tag) API.

#decision
Add EtherNet/IP gateway following the established gateway pattern:
- Model: IEnipGateway — host, port(44818), slot(0), timeout, tags(tagName/field/dataType)
- Manager: EnipGatewayManagerService — dynamic import of node-ethernet-ip, CIP tag reads
- Routes: /enip-gateways CRUD + /start /stop /test /status /read
- NATS publish: sensor.raw.${deviceId} with source='enip'
- slot: CPU slot in ControlLogix chassis (0–15); CompactLogix always 0

#consequences
~New package: node-ethernet-ip added to apps/api/package.json
~Tags identified by tagName string (PLC tag path); no numeric addresses
~dataType hint (REAL, DINT, INT, SINT, BOOL…) optional — CIP returns typed value natively
~If node-ethernet-ip not installed: dynamic import throws friendly error at startGateway
~Front-end: EnipGatewayTable/Modal/DetailPanel + useEnipGateways hook
~Sidebar: 'enip' entity item added to application sub-nav
~No impact on existing gateways or Processing Engine
